# Selective ownership — scalable by design.
#  • CONTENT docs need ONE peer approval from any write collaborator — no single-person
#    bottleneck. Deliberately NOT listed here.
#  • The SYSTEM layer below additionally requires the steward's review: these files define
#    how the system works (enforcement, protocol, structure map, standards, scope boundary).
#  • The machine-generated manifest is deliberately unowned — it regenerates on every change.
# Point at a TEAM (@your-org/your-docs-maintainers), never a person — ownership must transfer
# with a membership change, not a file change.

/scripts/                   @your-org/your-docs-maintainers
/.github/                   @your-org/your-docs-maintainers
/AGENTS.md                  @your-org/your-docs-maintainers
/CLAUDE.md                  @your-org/your-docs-maintainers
/README.md                  @your-org/your-docs-maintainers
/DOCS-STANDARD.md           @your-org/your-docs-maintainers
/DOCS-SYSTEM.md             @your-org/your-docs-maintainers
/delivery/CONVENTIONS.md    @your-org/your-docs-maintainers
